Task 3: Predictive Modeling - Linear Regression (Forecasting) 

Project Goal: 
To build a robust predictive model using Linear Regression for a continuous target variable (e.g., house price or sales demand), establishing a strong baseline for future regression tasks.
  
Key Outcomes & Skills:
a. Model Training: Developed a Multiple Linear Regression model on the preprocessed training data.
b. Performance Metrics: Evaluated the model using industry-standard regression metrics, achieving a low Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) and a high R-squared value, demonstrating strong predictive power.
c. Assumptions Validation: Performed critical residual analysis to verify that the model adheres to the fundamental assumptions of linearity and homoscedasticity, ensuring model reliability.
d. Coefficient Interpretation: Interpreted the model's coefficients to understand the relative impact of each independent variable on the predicted outcome, providing business-interpretable results.

Technical Stack
Category: Tool / Concept
Libraries: Scikit-learn (LinearRegression), NumPy
Concepts: Supervised Learning, Multiple Regression, RMSE/R-squared, Residual Plot Analysis, Baseline Model Establishment
